From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Recovery: enroll a board's padded Mach-O Stage 1 with
 kmutil --compress

The native Recovery app accepted raw mode only. It now also takes Mach-O mode
for a board whose engine contract stages Aura's Mach-O boot object (the
J714s on the 27.2 stub): install-config bootMode "macho" with the confined
Stage 2 m1n1/boot-ctxr.bin, payloads macho/aura-boot.macho (unpadded) and
macho/boot-ctxr.bin, and the manifest's executeWindow (128 MiB).

Before enrollment Recovery checks the object (no __TEXT_BOOT_EXEC, so iBoot
does not start SPTM), pads __TEXT_EXEC for the execute window as a sparse
file, checks what `kmutil inspect --show-mach-boot-properties` derives (kcbz
0 and the padded kcrz), then runs bputil -nc and
`kmutil configure-boot -c <padded> --compress -v <stub>`. The native PTY
prompt allows that one command 60 minutes (aurora-installer allows 30; Apple
says it may take 30). Verification, restart and `aura recover` use the
configured mode's Stage 2. The app selects the mode the installation
recorded.

MachOBootObject, ExecuteWindow, ExpandedMachOBootObject, the padding,
inspection and free-space checks and their fixture are ported from
aurora-silicon/aurora-installer (79a7549, MIT) Recovery/Sources/Account/
AuraStage1.swift, RecoveryActions.stageExpandedStage1, Native/Authorization.c
and Tests/MachOBootObjectCheck.swift.

Not compiled here (no Swift toolchain on this host); the native C check
(Tests/AuthorizationCheck.c) passes on Linux. The macOS CI builds and runs
Recovery/test-all.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
